  "notes" : [
    {
      "id" : "5EED0FD2-14D8-463C-897C-30F09DD8A73D",
      "note" : "# 3D Scene\n\nThis example expands on our concept of our composition and introduces a sense of space to our animation.\n\nWe introduce\n\n* A `Perspective Camera` to control our view of the scene.\n* A `Directional Light` to provide lighting to our scene.\n\nWe are familiar with `Geometry` , `Material` and `Mesh` nodes by now, but take note as to how each `Mesh` is positioned, and how different `Material` nodes respond to different lighting  and tranparency settings. \n\n\n### Next Steps\n* Play with the position of the `Camera Node` to get a sense for space. \n* Try animating the `Camera` position! You know how!\n* Play with the `Directional Lighting` node to get a sense for how different materials respond to lighting setups.\n* Try animating the `Directional Lighting` color or position for fun. ",
      "rect" : [
        [
          -909.142542693231,
          -834.184209893665
        ],
        [
          450.95565698170503,
          384.01281739367005
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
